  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "OptimizeByResampling",
    "file": "lcms/src/cmsopt.c",
    "description": "OptimizeByResampling accepts an explicit one-point grid encoded in dwFlags via _cmsReasonableGridpointsByColorspace() and passes nGridPoints == 1 to cmsStageAllocCLut16bit(). This creates a 3-D CLUT with Domain[] == 0 and only nOutputs table entries, although TetrahedralInterp16 assumes multidimensional CLUT axes have at least two nodes. During white-point evaluation, a channel that is not exactly 0xFFFF still produces a nonzero neighbor stride even though its domain is zero, so TetrahedralInterp16 reads a neighbor beyond the one-node table (the observed read at cmsintrp.c:767). OptimizeByResampling must reject or clamp an explicitly requested grid size below the minimum supported by its interpolator.",
    "conditions": "The harness derives flags, formats, and intent from the first 16 input bytes, then splits the remaining bytes into two ICC profiles and calls cmsCreateTransform. Triggering requires profiles/formats that produce a 3-input pipeline eligible for OptimizeByResampling, flags whose GRIDPOINTS field requests 1, and white-point fixup enabled (non-absolute intent and no cmsFLAGS_NOWHITEONWHITEFIXUP). Resampling allocates and samples a one-node CLUT; FixWhiteMisalignment then evaluates it at the colorspace white endpoint. Because at least one endpoint component is below 0xFFFF, TetrahedralInterp16 adds a neighbor stride despite Domain == 0 and reads past the CLUT allocation."
  },
